  "configuration_id": "config_002",
  "reason": "Evidence: Only two experiments are complete. RNA-only (pca_n2000, singleprofile) achieves 48.5% accuracy, while image-only (resnet50, singleprofile) is near-random at 20.8%, strongly indicating RNA is the dominant signal. Uncertainty: We have no information on whether multiprofile aggregation (capturing multiple cell profiles per sample) improves over a single profile. Question tested: config_002 isolates the profile/aggregation axis by keeping the same encoder (pca_n2000) as config_001 but switching to multiprofile with avgpool aggregation. This directly compares single-profile vs. multi-profile representation for the RNA modality. Why this is the best next experiment: Since RNA is clearly the primary signal, optimizing its configuration is the highest-leverage use of a limited budget. Testing multiprofile+avgpool is the simplest and most natural extension of the current best result, providing a clean one-variable comparison. If it improves, we gain a stronger RNA baseline before exploring multimodal fusion or more complex aggregations (transformer). If it does not, we rule out multi-profile benefit and can redirect effort toward encoder choice (scvi, scgpt) or multimodal fusion."
}

